# TUI-DESIGN-4 §7.3 item 6 / §10 S6: the boundaries that only render while a run is LIVE — `live`, `pane`,
# `overlay`. The shipped 4-step `--mock` trajectory leaves those slots closed, which is why `render:live` and
# `render:pane` never fired at 24×80 and the probe measured the unfaulted frame; this scenario starts a long run
# and forces the panel open, so the slot renders and the fault fires. One steps file, three JEVCODE_FAULT values
# (run-smoke.sh picks the value per scenario name).
#
# The exit is ONE Ctrl-C (abort the live run) and then `/exit`, never Ctrl-C twice: the second interrupt is
# EXIT_NOW_130 only while the run is still live, so a two-interrupt ending would race the run's own end and the
# scenario's exit code would depend on the machine's speed.
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.5
send start the fault run
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect \[run\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* started [·-] 
send /panel
sleep 0.2
send \r
sleep 2
send \x03
expect Follow-up, question|Say hi
sleep 0.4
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
